    <section id="mistakes">
      <h2>Mistakes that cause rejected Tally e-invoices</h2>
      <ul class="know">
        <li><b>Missing customer TRNs.</b> This is the most common problem. Run the Update Party TRN report and fix the gaps first.</li>
        <li><b>Names that do not match.</b> The customer's legal name must match its registration. A trading name will not do. Check your own too.</li>
        <li><b>Wrong units.</b> Free-text units may fail. Map every unit to the standard code.</li>
        <li><b>Items with no VAT treatment.</b> Every item needs the right treatment. Check each one in the VAT Rate Setup report.</li>
        <li><b>Discounts and charges with no reason.</b> UAE e-invoicing needs a reason whenever a discount, charge or excise amount changes the invoice value. Add the reason in Tally.</li>
        <li><b>Editing after sending.</b> You cannot. Credit notes fix mistakes. Check every invoice before you send it.</li>
        <li><b>Mixing B2B and B2C.</b> Do not send consumer receipts through Peppol. And do not skip a business customer. Mark customer types clearly.</li>
        <li><b>Letting TSS lapse.</b> Your e-invoicing stops. Renew before the date.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="know">
      <h2>Things to know before you start</h2>
      <ul class="know">
        <li><b>Keep TSS active.</b> E-invoicing in TallyPrime needs an active TSS subscription. Renew it before it lapses.</li>
        <li><b>Indian licences will need to change.</b> An Indian TallyPrime licence can be used for registration now. But Tally says registration will soon need an International licence. Plan the switch.</li>
        <li><b>Branches do not register again.</b> Once your head office is registered, branches can issue e-invoices under the same setup.</li>
        <li><b>Check the latest release.</b> Tally adds UAE features in new releases. Update before you start.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="help">
      <h2>Set it up yourself, or get help?</h2>
      <p>You can set up Tally yourself for free. The five steps above are enough for many businesses. If your customer and item data are clean, you may finish in an afternoon. Get help if your data is messy, if you have many customers or items, or if you have no time to test.</p>
      <p>Our setup service costs {aed(P.help)}, one time. We check your Tally release, TSS and Tally.NET ID. We check and fix your customer TRNs, VAT codes and items. We handle your EmaraTax appointment and registration. We send a test invoice and credit note. We fix any rejected invoice. And we show your staff how it works.</p>
      <p>Not on Tally? Other software has its own path. Zoho Books and Wafeq have e-invoicing built in, like Tally. QuickBooks and Excel need an outside ASP. See <a href="/zoho-books">Zoho Books</a>, <a href="/wafeq">Wafeq</a>, <a href="/quickbooks-online">QuickBooks Online</a> or <a href="/other-software">other software</a>. You can also read our <a href="/blog/zoho-e-invoicing-uae-guide">Zoho e-invoicing guide</a>.</p>
